python-activitytrack (0.9.4~beta5-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Security review fixes: the sync never dies on a refused address; no
    state write for an unchanged value; --dev allows http:// only for
    local addresses; the data folder's migration race; a certificate the
    library cannot read is a certificate error; keyring errors logged and
    the token file written as UTF-8 without following links; every
    thread's database connection closed.
  * cryptography >= 41.

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 18:53:45 +0100

python-activitytrack (0.9.4~beta4-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Dates and times as the user prefers them: European, American or ISO;
    24 or 12 hours (module formats, kept in the local copy for every
    interface; web issue #38).
  * The app's 5-minute time grid rules (module timegrid, Work.busy).
  * Without concurrent entries resuming an activity suspends the others,
    as a new start does (app issue #132).

 -- ActivityTrack <flavio-claude@zipman.it>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 15:50:04 +0100

python-activitytrack (0.9.4~beta3-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A Debian revision in the version, the distribution in it
    (0.9.4~beta3-1~deb13): 0.9.4~beta2~deb13 sorted before 0.9.4~beta2, so
    the interfaces' "(>= 0.9.4~beta2)" could not be satisfied. Source format
    3.0 (quilt), as the revision wants. Nothing else changes.

